  "interpretation": [
    "Candidate iteration in reuse_lazy_definition and rigid argument rejection together account for 22.08% of CPU self samples. Shared arena, substitution and hashing work adds cost but cannot be exclusively attributed from this sample report.",
    "Argument-list comparisons hit their existing cache 26036326 times out of 34336131 calls (75.8%). Reuse works, but too many candidates reach the comparison and cache lookup path.",
    "Definition candidates are scanned 63070578 times, and inductive candidates 9618575 times. Candidate vectors are indexed by original declaration, then scanned linearly.",
    "Detailed profiling attributes about 78.7% of accounted exclusive time to namespace operations. This includes profiling overhead and is not an uninstrumented runtime fraction.",
    "There are 6522905 unresolved comparisons, 1509512 failed kernel translations, and 5013393 avoided translation retries. A bounded follow-up emitted bound variable outside context as the first sampled kernel error kind. This does not establish the distribution of all failures.",
    "Both complete Tensor runs succeeded. Reuse-probe translation failures are provisional internal results, not reported user type errors.",
    "The definition-fresh counter counts lazy specialization records, not full kernel body checks; it must not be interpreted as repeated full typechecking.",
    "Only six kernel cache recycling events were recorded. The evidence prioritizes reducing repeated candidate exploration and comparison work; it does not measure the benefit of a different eviction policy."
  ],
  "proposed_priorities": [
    "Index candidates by arguments that are provably rigid. Keep a fallback for nonrigid expressions that may reduce to equal values; raw syntactic inequality is insufficient.",
    "Represent unresolved comparisons explicitly and share pending results across declarations with dependency-aware invalidation. Retry when needed context/materialization/remappings change; never permanently cache an unresolved result as unequal.",
    "Reuse interned argument IDs and alias-head results where validity can be established, avoiding repeated argument hashing and alias reduction."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Detailed cost collection increases runtime from 93.905 seconds in the sampled baseline to 123.189 seconds; these are different instrumentation modes, not an optimization comparison.",
    "Use exclusive times for decomposition. Recursive inclusive times overlap and must not be summed.",
    "No reliable caller attribution was obtained from the perf stack data; only self samples are reported.",
    "This investigation does not measure a complete differential_forms run or establish the cause of the originally reported 40-minute run.",
    "This change adds diagnostics only; candidate selection and equality algorithms are unchanged."
  ],
